cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below, and cite the paper."
title: "finite-avalanche: a Lean 4 formalization of Sandpile avalanches in two dimensions are finite"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the paper "Sandpile
  avalanches in two dimensions are finite" (Bou-Rabee): under the stationary
  law of the abelian sandpile on Z^2, adding one grain at the origin causes
  finitely many topplings almost surely, and the radius of the avalanche
  satisfies P(radius > M) <= C (log(M + 2))^(-a). All 17 numbered statements
  of the paper are proved; the proofs use 22 standard results from the
  literature, which enter as named axioms.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - abelian sandpile
  - uniform spanning tree
  - probability
license: Apache-2.0
